{
  "source": "Built from RefundCreateParams, the Refund object and the error object in the official stripe@23.1.0 type definitions (OpenAPI v2596), RQ-0104 S6 and RQ-0163; request encoding as RQ-0115 S6. Not recorded from a live account: no Stripe key or network was available. The key is one per approved refund document (lf-refund-v2-<refund id>, RQ-0163). Replace with a redacted test-mode recording (fixtures/recorded/) when one is (RQ-0104 follow-up). List Refunds (GET /v1/refunds?payment_intent=…&limit=100, paged by starting_after; RQ-0164 S1–S4) added 2026-11-15 from RefundListParams, PaginationParams and ApiList in the same SDK: before every create the send looks for a refund with metadata lf_refund_id. Security re-review R1 (2026-11-15): 'voided' interactions — the lookup must find a refund sent for a credit note voided afterwards; No interaction answers a second create for that document: it must never be requested.",
